From f0474e4bd6e6cd5015b65af0956e6dea751499a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 23:41:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/29] vndk.rc: force software codecs without disabling C2

the previous force_sw_codecs trigger set debug.stagefright.ccodec=0 to disable
C2 entirely. that was self-defeating: the AOSP software encoders such as
c2.android.avc.encoder are themselves C2 components, so disabling C2 made them
fail to allocate (createComponent -> OMITTED), leaving no AVC encoder at all
and turning "force software codecs" into "no codecs". users enabling the
toggle still hit error 7, but from missing-codec rather than PersistentSurface.

keep C2 enabled. the toggle now only sets debug.stagefright.c2inputsurface=-1
to activate the AIDL buffer-source fallback so a software encoder can still
create a PersistentSurface input on vendor kernels lacking the C2 input-surface
HAL. vendor hardware codec selection is handled by the matching MediaCodecList
filter (drop non-software codecs) and the OmxStore vendor-node filter, not by
disabling C2.

Relates-to: #33
Relates-to: #94
---
 vndk.rc | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vndk.rc b/vndk.rc
index 94c7583..ea4531c 100644
--- a/vndk.rc
+++ b/vndk.rc
@@ -136,3 +136,16 @@ service watchdogd-gsi /system/bin/watchdogd 10 20
 on property:persist.sys.phh.adb_secure=1
     exec u:r:phhsu_daemon:s0 root -- /system/bin/resetprop_phh ro.adb.secure 1
     restart adbd
+
+# force software codecs: keep C2 enabled (the AOSP software codecs such as
+# c2.android.avc.encoder are themselves C2 components, so disabling C2 would
+# also disable them) but route selection around vendor hardware via the
+# matching MediaCodecList filter, which drops non-software codecs when this
+# property is set. the OmxStore filter additionally drops vendor OMX nodes.
+# c2inputsurface=-1 activates the AIDL buffer-source fallback so a software
+# encoder can still create a PersistentSurface input for camera recording on
+# vendor kernels that lack the C2 input-surface HAL.
+# uses resetprop_phh -n to patch property area directly before media
+# services read them, matching the timing of CodecFix magisk module.
+on property:persist.sys.phh.force_sw_codecs=true
+    exec u:r:phhsu_daemon:s0 root -- /system/bin/resetprop_phh -n debug.stagefright.c2inputsurface -1
-- 
